  "docs": {
    "description": "Triggers an action — submits forms, confirms decisions, performs commands. Not for navigation (use Link), toggling (use Switch), or selecting options (use Checkbox/Radio).\n\nVariants (96):\n• size — xs (28px) | sm (36px) | md (44px, default) | lg (48px)\n• prio — primary | secondary | tertiary\n• state — default | hover | pressed | disabled\n• danger — false | true  (destructive/irreversible actions: delete, remove, revoke)\n\nFocus is not a variant — apply the shared effect style shadow/focus/default (or shadow/focus/danger on danger buttons) to the current state on :focus-visible.\n\nSizing: sm renders below the 44px WCAG touch target — pad the hit area in code. xs is reserved for ultra-dense contexts where the row or toolbar itself is the target.\n\nLabels: write as actions — \"Save changes\" not \"OK\", \"Delete project\" not \"Yes\". 1–3 words. Leading icon reinforces; trailing icon indicates direction; icon-only requires aria-label.\n\nRules: one primary per view. Danger is for destructive actions only — never for Cancel or Close. Never place two primary buttons side by side. Tertiary should not stand alone as the sole action.",
    "figmaIssues": [
      "Description says 96 variants; the set has 108.",
      "Axis `size`: description lists [xs, sm, md, lg], set has [md, sm, xl].",
      "Axis `state`: description lists [default, hover, pressed, disabled], set has [default, hover, pressed, disabled, focus, loading]."
    ]
  },
